WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.880
Speaker 1: This next story requires some explanation,
but it's pretty fascinating.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:12.820
A couple of days ago, Tucker Carlson, Fox
News propagandist, ran a kind of strange out

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:20.360
of place commentary on his show where he vaguely
referred to his college yearbooks and people

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.690
like Jeff Bezos looking for dirt on Tucker
Carlson.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.720
And it was weird because it was just out of
context.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.410
It seemed to have nothing to do with what
was going on on Tucker's show.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:33.640
And it raised the question of whether Tucker
Carlson was trying to get ahead of a maybe

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.449
embarrassing or problematic story.

00:00:36.449 --> 00:00:37.989
So let's start by taking a look at that.

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:40.620
This is the clip from a couple of nights ago,
just kind of out of nowhere.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.620
We don't know what this was about.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.030
Speaker 4: We're going to get a quick piece
of news from the world of big tech.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:48.270
We spent the day hearing from quite a few
old college classmates.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:51.280
In some cases people would be out of touch
with for 30 years.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.140
It was nice, but here was the occasion for
it.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:59.359
Jeff Bezos had one of his minions, a mentally
unbalanced, middle aged man called Erik Wemple,

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:03.389
poor, dusty college yearbook and call around
to see if we've done anything naughty at the

00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:04.389
age of 19.

00:01:04.389 --> 00:01:05.389
That sounds like fun.

00:01:05.389 --> 00:01:07.380
Let us know if you hear any good stories.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.829
But before Bezos drops any more of his billions
on opposition research, you should know that

00:01:11.829 --> 00:01:14.930
it will not affect any election outcome.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:15.930
This is a news show.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.780
It's not a political campaign.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:20.210
No one here is running for anything or plans
to.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:23.969
On the other hand, if Jeff Bezos wants to
come over to reminisce about nineteen eighty

00:01:23.969 --> 00:01:26.950
seven on this show, he's always welcome anytime.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:31.110
Speaker 1: Sort of a strange story in a vacuum.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:35.219
But then yesterday it all starts to become
much clearer.

00:01:35.219 --> 00:01:41.189
An image purporting to be Tucker Carlson's
college yearbook entry from Trinity College

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:47.359
in nineteen ninety one mentions that Tucker
was part of a number of groups, including

00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:54.869
the Christian Fellowship, OK, the Jesse Helms
Foundation, and something called the Dan White

00:01:54.869 --> 00:01:55.869
Society.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:02:00.929
Now, for those wondering whether this is even
a real image, Trinity College has confirmed

00:02:00.929 --> 00:02:04.259
that this is their real 1991 yearbook.

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:06.960
Tucker's entry is on page 186.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.830
There is no question about it being real.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:16.610
And this started to raise some questions because
the Dan White society references Dan White.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:23.269
Dan White was the guy who killed San Francisco
Mayor George Moscone and Supervisor Harvey

00:02:23.269 --> 00:02:28.330
Milk, California's first openly gay elected
official in 1978.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:33.280
Dan White was a horrible person, a disgustingly
violent, homophobic person.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.620
And so when you look at Tucker's yearbook
and it says Dan White society, that's starting

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.400
to look not so good.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.900
And then our longtime friend, Jeremy Hooper
did some more research into this and found

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:53.290
a 1990 op ed by Tucker Carlson in his college
newspaper where he calls homosexuality, quote,

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:56.150
unnatural and unhealthy.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:02.720
And it is signed TSM Carlson and indeed, Jeremy
confirmed that Tucker Carlson is the only

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.439
possible student with those initials at that
time.

00:03:06.439 --> 00:03:11.400
It also appears, as Jeremy Hooper points out
on Twitter, that this is the only thing Tucker.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.360
Ever wrote in the newspaper, meaning it's
not that Tucker was a regular columnist and

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:21.590
it just so happened that one day he wrote
about unnatural gay people, he went out of

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:28.689
his way to write one column one time about
his displeasure with the fact that gay people

00:03:28.689 --> 00:03:29.879
exist now.

00:03:29.879 --> 00:03:36.810
To me, this is less about whether Tucker Carlson
was homophobic in 1990 or 1991 as a sort of

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:40.690
potential disqualifier for Tucker to do whatever
today.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.159
First of all, there's tons of people that
are homophobic.

00:03:43.159 --> 00:03:47.060
Secondly, I don't think being homophobic is
considered a problem for Fox News host.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.510
That may even it may be a feature more than
it is a bug.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:57.610
And third, most importantly, in theory, Tucker's
views may have changed over the last 30 years.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:01.530
I have views that are different today than
they were 30 years ago.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:07.090
And much like I would say about anyone if
these were Tucker's views 30 years ago, and

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:11.110
they appear to be, it doesn't necessarily
tell us how his views are today.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:14.579
Many of my views have changed, although I
was never anti-gay.

00:04:14.579 --> 00:04:19.850
It's more about the strange nature of how
Tucker ended up getting into this story earlier

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:27.669
this week, doing this bizarre Proactiv segment
to attack Jeff Bezos and to say people are

00:04:27.669 --> 00:04:28.920
looking for dirt.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.870
It's just all very strange.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:36.300
Now, that being said, yeah, Tucker's heroes
in college were really disturbing.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:42.949
It's not just that of the three groups he
mentions, one seems to be an adoration of

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:46.630
the guy who killed Harvey Milk for being gay.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:48.350
That's horrifying.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.740
He also shouts out Jesse Helms.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:57.780
Jesse Helms used to be a senator who opposed
the Civil Rights Act, opposed the Voting Rights

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:02.610
Act, called the Civil Rights Act, dangerous
and on and on.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:07.740
If these were Tucker's heroes, then I'd be
curious as to who his heroes are today.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.050
It's really horrible stuff.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.910
I don't expect much more to come of it.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:14.030
You know, anybody thought, oh, he should be
fired from Fox News.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.230
Yeah, right.

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:20.300
Even if Fox News doesn't see this as a feature,
it's not going to cause a problem for Tucker

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:24.810
on Fox News, but a very strange story and
watching it develop it, watching it develop

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:26.160
over the week.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.570
Even stranger with the Proactiv.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:30.280
Oh, people are calling around looking for
dirt on me.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.280
Really weird.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:31.740
Let me know what you make of it

